item.description:
Third Way is a national think tank and advocacy organization that champions moderate policy and political ideas. Since our founding in 2005, we have served as a critical bulwark against political extremism by advancing values-driven, reform-oriented solutions on the defining issues of our time. Our work is grounded in the mainstream American values of opportunity, freedom, security, and democratic capitalism, and we advocate for the vital center across seven major areas: climate and energy, economy, education, health care, national security, politics, and social policy.
Third Way’s climate and energy program advocates for policies that rapidly deploy the technologies needed to decarbonize and lower costs across the United States. By focusing on what matters most to everyday Americans, we are growing the clean energy coalition.
Our team is seeking a
Digital Design Intern
to strengthen our online presence. The perfect candidate will have the creative eye, technical expertise, and cultural savvy needed to leverage important moments and generate attention-grabbing content. The Digital Design Intern will support policy and political work by translating complex information into clear and accessible multimedia products.
A typical day for the Digital Design Intern could include:
Creating social media graphics and videos;
Developing templates to bolster rapid response efforts;
Researching competitors and emerging design trends;
Supporting communications processes and organizing design assets;
Attending relevant team meetings;
Participating in intern cohort programming and events.
*
Applications close on August 10, 2026. Internship offers will be extended between August 17 and August 21, 2026.*
*Please note all duties and events will require in-office participation. This is a part-time, PAID INTERNSHIP. *

Third Way is a national think tank and advocacy organization that champions moderate policy and political ideas. Since our founding in 2005, we have served as a critical bulwark against political extremism by advancing values-driven, reform-oriented solutions on the defining issues of our time. Our work is grounded in the mainstream American values of opportunity, freedom, security, and democratic capitalism, and we advocate for the vital center across seven major areas: climate and energy, economy, education, health care, national security, politics, and social policy.
Third Way's Business Operations Department (
BizOps
) seeks an energetic, motivated, and dedicated
Operations and Projects Intern
with exceptional communication and writing skills to work alongside our Business Operations Team and Senior Project Advisor on related projects. We offer an opportunity to work in a dynamic, forward-thinking organization that promotes center-left ideas. The intern's primary responsibility is to help manage projects and assist with assigned projects' administrative, technical, and financial aspects. The Intern will report directly to the Senior Project Advisor (SPA).
As an
Operations and Projects Intern,
you will acquire practical experience in planning, executing, and monitoring projects, enhancing your project management and organizational skills. You will learn to coordinate cross-functional teams, manage project timelines, and meet deliverables. Additionally, you will gain expertise in using project management tools and methodologies to drive operational efficiency and project success. You will learn to collaborate across departments, manage projects, and support strategic initiatives to drive operational efficiency across the Business Operation Team. In addition, you’ll have the opportunity to learn from other members of the Business Operation Team. We aim for you to have a well-rounded project and business operations internship.
As a BizOps Intern, a typical day might include…
Project & Task Management:
Reviewing, creating, and/or maintaining workflows to drive effectiveness on
Monday.com
;
Effectively contributing and thriving in a collaborative, team-oriented work environment;
Supporting team leads on cross-departmental initiatives;
Managing assigned project tasks through completion;
Coordinating and communicating on interdepartmental tasks and processes;
Ensuring quality and timely submission of all project deliverables and documentation as assigned by the SPA;
Managing and updating project progress on
Monday.com
, ensuring all information is current;
Handling email correspondence related to assigned projects and initiatives;
Participating in brief daily check-ins with the SPA to outline the day’s priorities, and weekly check-ins to discuss open projects and upcoming events;
Ensuring all technological and physical space setups are ready for any meetings, events, or presentations scheduled for the day;
Office Maintenance & Administrative Support:
Providing high-level customer service to all TW staff and visitors;
Assisting as needed in maintaining organization/tidiness of all common areas (i.e. Pantry, Workroom, Huddle Booths, Conference Rooms, Reception Area);
Performing other job-related duties as requested for the BizOps Team;
Meetings & Events: Health & Wellness and Center For Fun (Quarterly, with Ongoing Weekly Planning):
Conducting research on availability, manage scheduling invitations, and coordinate logistics like catering and materials;
Helping set up and break down rooms for Center for Fun (CFF) and Health & Wellness (H&W) events and activities;
Tracking and documenting event logistics, attendance, and feedback for future improvements;
Sending out save-the-date and full invitation emails and coordinate meeting logistics;
Short-Term Projects
Long-Term Projects:
Internal Process Audit & Optimization Toolkit:
Audit existing internal process (e.g., onboarding, meeting scheduling, project intake, or task tracking), identify inefficiencies, and create a clear, replicable
Process Optimization Toolkit
(including documentation, templates, and recommendations) to streamline and improve that process for future use;
Phase 1 – Process Selection & Stakeholder Interviews
Choose one core BizOps process (can be assigned or selected with your guidance);
Conduct interviews or shadow relevant team members to understand the workflow;
Document the current state using flowcharts or visual diagrams (use Miror or
monday.com
boards);
Phase 2 – Pain Point Identification & Benchmarking
Phase 3 –Solution Proposals
Phase 4 - Toolkit Development
Create SOPs, templates, or checklists to support the new process;
Build a sample workflow in
monday.com
(if relevant);
Phase 5 - Capstone Presentation
*
Applications close on August 10, 2026. Internship offers will be extended between August 17 and August 21, 2026. *
*Please note all duties and events will require in-office participation. This is a part-time, PAID INTERNSHIP. *
